      "side": 1,
      "message": "i\u0027m not keen on this AI slop of every math instruction needing asserts.  It makes the code harder to understand and maintain.\nThis is a low level internal function.  should really be static.  the public facing calling code, where parameters come from an untrusted source, should be checked?\nif ubsan is catching a bug, it means the source of the issue is the unittest or the public function?  perhaps this is a reason we should remove row tests?\n\nI\u0027d prefer the asserts all be the first thing in the function, all together and when necessary a matching if statement so the optimized build that does not assert, will avoid a crash and safely return without doing any work.",
