      "writtenOn": "2026-08-14T21:25:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ideally this would compute the scale factor is exactly an odd integer (3).  and use linear for them all. eg 5, 7, 9.\n\nfor example you can do this:\nbool is_ratio_odd(int a, int b) {\n    // 1. Division by zero check\n    if (b \u003d\u003d 0) return false; \n    \n    // 2. Performance check: if \u0027a\u0027 cannot be divided evenly by \u0027b\u0027\n    if (a % b !\u003d 0) return false; \n    \n    // 3. Ultra-fast bitwise check for odd ratio\n    // (a \u0026 -a) extracts the lowest set bit (trailing zeros / power of 2)\n    return (a \u0026 -a) \u003d\u003d (b \u0026 -b);\n}",
      "revId": "614a71f21d79d95929ef38c45cacf397b1c11897",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
